# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

@AGENTS.md

`AGENTS.md` is the contract for this repository and it is complete on its own. This file
exists because Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`; it deliberately adds nothing substantive,
so that a Codex or Gemini session — which reads `AGENTS.md` and never sees this file — is
working from the same instructions rather than a subset.

## Claude Code affordances

Hooks, `.claude/settings.json` permissions, and subagents work here and do nothing on the
other CLIs. Nothing in this project's gates depends on them: `node scripts/gate.mjs` is
the gate, and it behaves identically everywhere including CI.

If you add something Claude-only that a reviewer would need, it belongs in `AGENTS.md`
with a note that it is Claude-only — not here, where two thirds of the tools cannot see
it.

